@node Identifiers
@subsection Identifiers

Identifiers refer to variables, properties, or methods. All identifiers are normalized to
PascalCase.

@example
x
playerName
health
@end example

@node Binary Operations
@subsection Binary Operations

@table @code
@item +
Addition: @code{x + y}

@item -
Subtraction: @code{x - y}

@item *
Multiplication: @code{x * y}

@item /
Division: @code{x / y}

@item ==
Equality: @code{x == y}

@item !=
Inequality: @code{x != y}

@item <
Less than: @code{x < y}

@item >
Greater than: @code{x > y}

@item <=
Less or equal: @code{x <= y}

@item >=
Greater or equal: @code{x >= y}

@item &&
Logical AND: @code{x && y}

@item ||
Logical OR: @code{x || y}
@end table

@node Unary Operations
@subsection Unary Operations

@table @code
@item -
Negation: @code{-x}

@item !
Logical NOT: @code{!x}
@end table

@node Precedence
@subsection Precedence

Operator precedence (lowest to highest):
@enumerate
@item @code{||}
@item @code{&&}
@item @code{!}, @code{-}
@item @code{==}, @code{!=}, @code{<}, @code{<=}, @code{>}, @code{>=}
@item @code{+}, @code{-}
@item @code{*}, @code{/}
@item Assignment (@code{=}) — right-associative
@end enumerate

@node Control Structures
@section Control Structures

@menu
* if Statement::
* while Statement::
* for Statement::
* break Statement::
* continue Statement::
@end menu

@node if Statement
@subsection if Statement

@subheading Purpose and Function

The @code{if} statement evaluates a condition and executes one of two statement blocks.

@subheading Syntax

@example
IF condition THEN
    statements
END

IF condition THEN
    statements
ELSE
    statements
END
@end example

@subheading Examples

@example
IF x > 0 THEN
    x = x - 1
END

IF health <= 0 THEN
    [self die]
ELSE
    health = health - damage
END
@end example

@subheading Output

Maps to EightBol's @code{:if} node.

@node while Statement
@subsection while Statement

@subheading Purpose and Function

The @code{while} statement loops while a condition is true.

@subheading Syntax

@example
WHILE condition DO
    statements
END
@end example

@subheading Examples

@example
WHILE x < 10 DO
    x = x + 1
END

WHILE [sprite isActive] DO
    [sprite update]
END
@end example

@subheading Output

Maps to EightBol's @code{:perform :until} construct.

@node for Statement
@subsection for Statement

@subheading Purpose and Function

The @code{for} statement iterates a variable from a start value to an end value.

@subheading Syntax

@example
FOR ident = number TO number DO
    statements
END
@end example

@subheading Examples

@example
FOR i = 0 TO 10 DO
    DISPLAY i
END

FOR j = 1 TO 100 DO
    score = score + j
END
@end example

@subheading Output

Maps to EightBol's @code{:perform :varying} construct.

@node break Statement
@subsection break Statement

@subheading Purpose and Function

@code{break} exits the innermost enclosing loop.

@subheading Syntax

@example
break;
@end example

@subheading Examples

@example
FOR i = 0 TO 100 DO
    IF i = target THEN
        break;
    END
END
@end example

@node continue Statement
@subsection continue Statement

@subheading Purpose and Function

@code{continue} skips to the next iteration of the enclosing loop.

@subheading Syntax

@example
continue;
@end example

@node Input/Output Statements
@section Input/Output Statements

@menu
* DISPLAY::
* ACCEPT::
* SPEAK::
* COPY::
@end menu

@node DISPLAY
@subsection DISPLAY

@subheading Purpose and Function

@code{DISPLAY} outputs text or values to the console or output stream.

@subheading Syntax

@example
DISPLAY expression, expression, ...;
@end example

@subheading Examples

@example
DISPLAY "Hello, World!";
DISPLAY "Score: ", score;
DISPLAY "X=", x, " Y=", y;
@end example

@subheading Output

Maps to EightBol's @code{:print} node.

@node ACCEPT
@subsection ACCEPT

@subheading Purpose and Function

@code{ACCEPT} reads input from the user into a variable.

@subheading Syntax

@example
ACCEPT variableName;
@end example

@subheading Examples

@example
ACCEPT playerName;
ACCEPT guess;
@end example

@subheading Output

Maps to EightBol's @code{:input} node.

@node SPEAK
@subsection SPEAK

@subheading Purpose and Function

@code{SPEAK} displays dialogue text, typically for game character speech.

@subheading Syntax

@example
SPEAK expression, expression, ...;
@end example

@subheading Examples

@example
SPEAK "Hello, adventurer!";
SPEAK "You have ", health, " health remaining.";
@end example

@subheading Output

Maps to EightBol's @code{:dialogue} node.

@node COPY
@subsection COPY

@subheading Purpose and Function

@code{COPY} includes another source file (copybook) at compile time.

@subheading Syntax

@example
COPY "filename";
@end example

@subheading Examples

@example
COPY "game-constants.cpy";
COPY "sprite-definitions.cpy";
@end example

@subheading Output

Maps to EightBol's @code{:copy} node for copybook inclusion.

@node Identifier Normalization
@section Identifier Normalization

The Objective-C frontend automatically normalizes all identifiers to PascalCase during
lexing. The first character is converted to uppercase; subsequent characters are converted
to lowercase. Leading and trailing underscores are trimmed.

@subheading Examples

@multitable @columnfractions 0.3 0.3 0.4
@headitem Source @tab Normalized @tab Notes
@item @code{myVariable} @tab @code{Myvariable} @tab First char uppercase
@item @code{MY_CONST} @tab @code{My_const} @tab Underscore preserved
@item @code{_private} @tab @code{Private} @tab Leading underscore trimmed
@item @code{className} @tab @code{Classname} @tab camelCase to PascalCase
@end multitable

@node Unsupported Features
@section Unsupported Features

The Objective-C frontend intentionally omits certain features to match EightBol's 8-bit/16-bit
target constraints:

@itemize
@item Preprocessor directives (beyond @code{@} keywords)
@item Exception handling (@code{@try}, @code{@catch}, @code{@finally}, @code{@throw}) —
  replaced with fault logging
@item Automatic Reference Counting (ARC)
@item Blocks and Grand Central Dispatch
@item Floating-point types (@code{float}, @code{double})
@item Variadic methods
@item @code{@protocol} formal protocol declarations
@item Category and extension declarations
@item Method signatures with @code{self} and @code{super} in parameter types
@item @code{id<Protocol>} typed message sends
@item Selector variable types (@code{SEL})
@item Message forwarding
@item @code{@try} blocks for exception handling
@end itemize

Features like exception handling are replaced with fault logging via @code{:log-fault}
nodes in the AST.

@node Summary
@section Summary

This chapter has documented the complete Objective-C frontend language:

@itemize
@item Class definitions: @code{@@interface}, @code{@@implementation}, @code{@@end}
@item Property management: @code{@@property}, @code{@@synthesize}, @code{@dynamic}
@item Methods: instance methods (@code{-}), class methods (@code{+})
@item Message send: @code{[object method:arg]}
@item Control flow: @code{IF/THEN/ELSE/END}, @code{WHILE/DO/END}, @code{FOR/TO/DO/END}
@item Statements: @code{local}, assignment, @code{return}, @code{break}, @code{continue}
@item I/O: @code{DISPLAY}, @code{ACCEPT}, @code{SPEAK}, @code{COPY}
@item Expressions: arithmetic, relational, logical operators
@item Number formats: decimal, hex, octal, binary, dword
@item Identifier normalization: PascalCase
@end itemize

For implementation details, see @file{src/frontend-objective/objective-lexer.lisp} and
@file{src/frontend-objective/objective-parser.lisp}.
